cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its source data, please cite the accompanying paper and this archive."
title: "Code and source data for 'Vehicles missed by failed cameras reshape urban traffic recovery estimates after a typhoon'"
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Zengzhi-Zhang/shangyu-typhoon-capture"
abstract: >-
  During Typhoon In-Fa (July 2021), many licence-plate recognition cameras in
  Shangyu, China, stopped recording or missed part of the passing traffic. The
  accompanying study linked GPS traces of 290 taxis to the camera records to
  measure, camera by camera, the share of taxi passages each camera recorded,
  and showed how the choice of which cameras to trust changes estimates of
  network recovery. This archive contains the analysis code, the figure source
  data, public map layers and a synthetic dataset. The camera records and taxi
  traces are restricted and are not included.
